    "result_text": "AcceptanceTest is the only test class, and both tests pass. The full build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `membershipTier` field on owners: **`SILVER`** when `namesakeCount` is 0 and an email is present, otherwise **`BRONZE`**.\n\nFollowing the existing derived-field pattern (`membershipNumber`, `customerCode`), the changes are:\n\n1. **`MembershipTier.java`** (new) \u2014 a stateless helper in the owner function package with `of(Integer namesakeCount, String email)` returning `\"SILVER\"`/`\"BRONZE\"`. It treats a null count or blank/null email as not qualifying, so legacy owners degrade safely to `BRONZE`.\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `@Mapping` expression wiring `membershipTier` to `MembershipTier.of(owner.getNamesakeCount(), owner.getEmail())`, mirroring the `membershipNumber` mapping.\n\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `membershipTier` string property to the `Owner` schema (kept as a plain string, not an enum, so the mapper's `String`-returning expression matches the generated setter).\n\nThe tier is derived on read, so it flows through the existing `GET /api/owners/{id}` responder (`RespondWithOwner`) that the acceptance tests exercise. Both new tests (`coreSilverWhenUniqueWithEmail`, `functionalityBronzeWhenNoEmail`) pass and the full build is green.",
